    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on thompson1917-ch01-08: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.05";
    dc:description "This is a conceptual claim about categories. No dataset of organismal properties can show that a clear vital-versus-physical rule is impossible, because any proposed rule can be rejected as unclear without a measurable consequence that separates the claim from a rival rule.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The claim asserts that there is no clear rule dividing vital from physical properties. A survey of how biologists classify phenomena would describe usage, not confirm or refute the absence of a rule.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Denying a classification does not specify a distinguishing measurement.";
